{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce9ewvc6t1sePwA7xao99","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015AonsPZo3CbgSCYSiDX3vF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.YnESQc/Q-REPORT.md","content":"# Quarterly operations report — Q2 FY2026 (May–July 2026)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe quarter opened strong and lost momentum as it went on. Revenue rose from €412,380 in May to €431,205 in June (+4.6%), then fell to €389,640 in July (-9.6%), landing the quarter at €1,233,225 in total revenue against €467,640 in costs, for a net of €765,585 and a healthy 62.1% margin. Customer growth told a similar story: net adds were positive every month but shrank steadily, from +69 in May to +52 in June to +32 in July, as new signings slowed and churn climbed. Support held up well, closing 95.5% of the 1,001 tickets opened over the quarter, though the team closed fewer tickets than it opened in each individual month.\n\n## Key figures\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Quarterly revenue | €1,233,225 |\n| Quarterly costs | €467,640 |\n| Net | €765,585 |\n| Margin | 62.1% |\n| Net customer adds | 153 |\n| Ticket close rate | 95.5% |\n| June revenue growth | 4.6% |\n| July revenue growth | -9.6% |\n\n## Notes\n\nNew customer signings declined each month (86 → 74 → 63) while churn rose (17 → 22 → 31), so the net-adds slowdown is a two-sided trend worth watching heading into Q3. Costs held roughly flat month to month (€151k–€158k) even as revenue swung, so July's margin compression was driven entirely by the revenue drop rather than cost growth. Marketing spend dipped in July (€16,980, down from €21,400 in June) alongside the fall-off in new signings — worth checking whether the two are connected. Support opened more tickets than it closed in every month of the quarter, leaving a small but persistent backlog (45 tickets over the quarter) despite the strong overall close rate.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_r